# Test: fib-vpp programs a 2-path BGP ECMP route into VPP via the GoVPP stub
# and atomically updates it to 1 path when one ECMP member is withdrawn.
#
# Question: when two equal-cost BGP routes for 10.20.0.0/24 (next hops
# 10.0.0.11 and 10.0.0.12, both covered by dummy vpp-ecmp0 10.0.0.2/24) are
# injected into bgp-rib under `bgp { multipath { maximum-paths 4; } }`, does
# the full daemon pipeline (bgp-rib -> sysrib -> fib-vpp -> GoVPP wire) send an
# ip_route_add_del_v2 with is_add=true, n_paths=2 and both next hops, and when
# 10.0.0.11 is withdrawn does fib-vpp send an is_add=true update with n_paths=1
# and 10.0.0.12 with no intervening is_add=false withdrawal? A unit test exercises
# fib-vpp alone; only the daemon proves bgp-rib multipath selection, sysrib ECMP
# resolution against a VPP connected route, and GoVPP wire framing end-to-end.
#
# Flow: the compiled driver starts the VPP stub on a per-test Unix socket with
# a JSONL request log, then ze with vpp.external, connected {}, dummy vpp-ecmp0
# (10.0.0.2/24), bgp multipath, fib.vpp.enabled=true, and the observer plugin.
# The observer waits for bgp-rib, fib-vpp, and the 10.0.0.0/24 connected cover,
# injects both BGP paths, verifies the 2-path stub entry, withdraws 10.0.0.11,
# verifies the 1-path update for 10.0.0.12 with no delete between them, and
# shuts ze down cleanly.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-fib-depth AC-5 (VPP multi-path FibPath programming),
#            AC-14 (ECMP member failure updates route without full withdrawal)
# PREVENTS:  sysrib ECMP paths dropped before fib-vpp, or fib-vpp emitting a
#            withdraw before replacing a shrinking ECMP group on VPP.

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture vpp/vpp-fib-ecmp:timeout=30s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:pattern=OK: fib-vpp programmed 2-path ECMP and updated to 1-path for 10.20.0.0/24
